You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# OTP Input (`otp-input`)

One-time-code input: digits pop into cells, a caret blinks in the active cell, wrong codes shake and clear, right codes turn green.

## What it should do
Build an OTP input backed by ONE transparent real `<input autocomplete="one-time-code" inputMode="numeric">` stretched over N visual cells (so paste and SMS autofill work). Typed digits pop in with a bouncy spring; the active cell shows a ring and blinking caret; on completion call onComplete — false → horizontal shake keyframes [0,-10,10,-7,7,-3,0], red cells, clear; true → green cells.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/otp-input.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).
- Motion tokens go at `lib/kinetik/tokens.ts` (source below). Use tokens instead of magic numbers.

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** A single real input (autocomplete=one-time-code, inputMode numeric) powers the cells, so paste, SMS autofill and screen readers just work. Reduced motion: no shake.
- **Performance:** Only the changed digit animates.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

